    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d192">

                <pb facs="0406" n="360" xml:id="pg360"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/1602½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">18 April, 1918</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I would very much value
                    a memorandum containing <hi rendition="#underline">all</hi> that we know about
                    these several <hi rendition="#underline">nuclei</hi> of self-governing authority
                    that seem to be springing up in Siberia. It would afford me a great deal of
                    satisfaction to get behind the most nearly representative of them if it can
                    indeed draw leadership and control to itself. A summary of what we know
                    (stripped of the confusions of the cables) would be a most welcome thing as a
                    support to my judgment in the premises.</p>
                <p>Faithfully Yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
